{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Hollow with boards you shall make it.</b> It was square, for so it is written, ״רבוע יהיה״, and the boards were of acacia wood for its four sides, and hollow in the middle. And so Onkelos translated: חליל לוחין, which is from the language of (Job 11:12) ״ואיש נבוב ילבב״ — for a person in his childhood is hollow, devoid of knowledge and understanding, and afterward ילבב, meaning he acquires a heart." "<b>And behold,</b> in the hollow of this altar they would fill it with earth at the time of their encampment, in order to offer upon it; and this is what is written (Exodus 20:21): ״מזבח אדמה תעשה לי״. And this altar was a great miracle wrought in its workings: the fire burned in it day and night, and the wood was not consumed and the copper was not melted. And among the miracles that were in the Temple is that the fire of this altar was never extinguished by rains, and it was placed in the courtyard in an exposed place, in the manner of the court of the Tabernacle within the Tabernacle. And they said in the Midrash: Moses was afraid lest the fire consume the wood of the altar. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: Moses, why are you afraid? Who commanded the fire to consume? Learn from yourself: when you entered into the cloud of fire and walked among battalions of fire, and not only that, but you came to Me, as it is said (Exodus 20:18): ״ומשה נגש אל הערפל אשר שם האלהים״ — and My glory is a consuming fire, as it is said (Deuteronomy 4:24): ״כי ה׳ אלהיך אש אוכלה הוא״, and you were not consumed. So too the copper altar, even though it is written of it (Leviticus 6:6): ״אש תמיד תוקד על המזבח לא תכבה״ — the copper was not melted and the wood was not consumed. And if you should say that its plating was thick — R. Nehemiah said: its thickness was a dinar. R. Pinchas son of Hama said: the altar that Moses made was more beloved than the altar that Solomon made, but the altar that Solomon made was larger, as it is said (1 Kings 3:4): ״אלף עולות יעלה שלמה על המזבח ההוא״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:04:57.594483462Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}